# Copy to .env:  Copy-Item env.example .env  (PowerShell)

# --- PostgreSQL (required) ---
# Local Docker Postgres (from backend folder): npm run db:up
# If port 5432 is already in use on your machine, set POSTGRES_PORT=5433 (or another free host port) in .env.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mydetailos:mydetailos@localhost:5432/mydetailos?schema=public
#
# Neon / hosted Postgres — paste connection string; use ssl if required.
# If the URL contains channel_binding=require and Render/your host fails with generic "Internal Server Error",
# the API strips it automatically — you can also remove it in Neon when copying the URI.

JWT_SECRET=my-detail-os-dev-jwt-secret
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
PORT=4000

# Swagger / OpenAPI UI at GET /api/docs (spec: /api/docs/openapi.json).
# Default: enabled when NODE_ENV is not production; disabled in production.
# Set true to force-enable in production (not recommended on public hosts).
# SWAGGER_ENABLED=true
# SWAGGER_ENABLED=false

# Browser origin(s) allowed by CORS. Production = your Vercel URL (no trailing slash).
# Browser origin(s) allowed by CORS. Comma-separated list. No trailing slash.
# Local dev (both frontends):
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001,http://localhost:3002,http://localhost:3003
# Production:
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=https://my-detail-os-website.vercel.app,https://www.mydetailos.com,https://app.mydetailos.com,https://admin.mydetailos.com
# First origin is used for staff password-reset links (workshop app).

# Profile avatars + job-card inspection photos (before/after) — choose ONE:
#
# A) Local disk (default): files under backend/uploads (avatars/, job-cards/…); DB stores `/uploads/...`.
#    Fine for local dev. On Render, disk is ephemeral — images can disappear on restart.
#
# B) S3-compatible cloud (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO): set ALL of these on the API to skip local disk:
#
# S3_BUCKET=my-bucket
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://pub-xxxxx.r2.dev
# S3_REGION=auto
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
#
# Bucket / IAM: allow PutObject (and optional DeleteObject) under prefixes `avatars/*`, `job-cards/*`, and `branding/*`.
# For public image URLs via `S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, grant GetObject on those prefixes (same pattern as avatars).
#
# AWS-only quick setup (fills bucket policy + turns off bucket Block Public Access):
#   Fill S3_BUCKET, S3_REGION, S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID, S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY — leave S3_ENDPOINT unset.
#   IAM user needs: s3:PutBucketPolicy, s3:GetBucketPolicy, s3:PutPublicAccessBlock, s3:GetPublicAccessBlock on this bucket.
#   npm run s3:setup-aws-public-read
#   If IAM denies PutBucketPublicAccessBlock: turn Block Public Access OFF in S3 console for the bucket,
#   then: npm run s3:setup-aws-policy-only   (or npm run s3:setup-aws-public-read -- --policy-only)
#   IAM template: scripts/iam-s3-setup-policy.example.json (replace bucket name in Resource ARNs).
#   If browsers still get AccessDenied, turn off Block Public Access at ACCOUNT level (S3 sidebar → account settings).
#   Dry run: npm run s3:setup-aws-public-read -- --dry-run
#
# Inspection files use private `inspection-assets/*` and `inspection-reports/*` keys;
# grant the API PutObject, GetObject, and DeleteObject only for those prefixes.
# Inspection files are never served via S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL. Local development stores them in private_uploads/.
# API_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://api.yourdomain.com

# =============================================================================
# Twilio — SMS + WhatsApp (all optional; omit to use console OTP + dev bypass)
# Console: https://console.twilio.com
# =============================================================================
#
# --- Account (required for real SMS or WhatsApp) ---
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# --- Auth — use ONE of these (not both needed in .env): ---
# Primary auth token (Account → API keys & tokens → Auth Token):
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token_here
#
# OR API key (recommended for production; Key type “Standard”, SID starts with SK):
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=SKxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=your_api_key_secret_here
#
# --- SMS (login OTP and transactional SMS) ---
# Your Twilio SMS-enabled number, E.164 (US trial often +1…; must be verified on trial):
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+15555551234
#
# When users enter a 10-digit national number, the API prepends this (India default +91):
# TWILIO_TO_NUMBER_PREFIX=+91
# For US-only users you might use: TWILIO_TO_NUMBER_PREFIX=+1
#
# --- WhatsApp (messaging API routes & Login OTP; same Twilio Account SID + token or API key as above) ---
# Sender must be WhatsApp-enabled in Twilio:
#   • Sandbox: Twilio gives a number like +1 415 523 8886 — use exactly as below.
#   • Production: your approved WhatsApp Business sender (often whatsapp:+country…).
# Prefix can be “whatsapp:+14155238886” or “+14155238886” (code normalizes to whatsapp:…).
# TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM=whatsapp:+14155238886
#
# Approved WhatsApp Authentication template (Content SID: HX...) for Login OTP.
# Twilio Content Template parameter {{1}} is mapped to the one-time login code.
# TWILIO_OTP_TEMPLATE_SID=HXx...
#
# Channel preference for Login OTP ('whatsapp' | 'sms' | 'auto'). Defaults to 'auto'.
# When set to 'whatsapp', OTP is strictly sent via WhatsApp only (no SMS fallback).
# OTP_DELIVERY_CHANNEL=whatsapp
#
# Set false to disable SMS OTP delivery while India DLT approval is pending (defaults to true).
# OTP_SMS_ENABLED=false
#
# =============================================================================
# Twilio WhatsApp Content Template SIDs (Pre-approved)
# =============================================================================
# TWILIO_CUSTOMER_WELCOME_CONTENT_SID=HX2656ed64ee960fb6995f9211b4b71c72
# TWILIO_AUTH_OTP_CONTENT_SID=HXf1c8e1cbd228b0ab0700445712169f1e
# TWILIO_SERVICE_REMINDER_CONTENT_SID=HX7eb233c8252b14bee9403c8eb4bd1fea
# TWILIO_PAYMENT_PENDING_CONTENT_SID=HX429538b3d8638a6ef9c0aff78dc0c933
# TWILIO_INSPECTION_REPORT_CONTENT_SID=HXe3ca0b811651060e2d338d598eef2270
# TWILIO_JOB_CARD_CREATED_CONTENT_SID=HXbc4e0ac2bdef379fe6acc1b3a7f128c1
# TWILIO_JOB_CARD_READY_CONTENT_SID=HX67fe4e7fead33acd40e482197767bdf8
# TWILIO_INVOICE_CREATED_CONTENT_SID=HX80046e56ada2f400631a63e821f530f9
# TWILIO_PAYMENT_RECEIVED_CONTENT_SID=HX8f6f9a652fe4e845e48f3305d3a212d3
# TWILIO_JOB_DELIVERED_CONTENT_SID=HXf36d3b11526768d4623e917fd9b52b3c
#
# Legacy alias keys (also supported):
# TWILIO_JOB_CARD_CREATED_TEMPLATE_SID=HXbc4e0ac2bdef379fe6acc1b3a7f128c1
# TWILIO_INSPECTION_TEMPLATE_SID=HXe3ca0b811651060e2d338d598eef2270
# TWILIO_SERVICE_REMINDER_TEMPLATE_SID=HX7eb233c8252b14bee9403c8eb4bd1fea
# TWILIO_PAYMENT_PENDING_TEMPLATE_SID=HX429538b3d8638a6ef9c0aff78dc0c933
# TWILIO_CUSTOMER_PORTAL_TEMPLATE_SID=HX2656ed64ee960fb6995f9211b4b71c72
# TWILIO_OTP_TEMPLATE_SID=HXf1c8e1cbd228b0ab0700445712169f1e
#
# Additional SaaS platform templates:
# TWILIO_OWNER_PLAN_ACTIVATED_TEMPLATE_SID=HX6614aca21b384ae0eb0089e30eb11981
# TWILIO_OWNER_PAYMENT_LINK_TEMPLATE_SID=HX1bede6b642ec0b693a58bb793bb99558
# TWILIO_OWNER_TRIAL_STARTED_TEMPLATE_SID=HXe75d4fd3589625f967fd09cb3dd4cad8
#
# Recipients: in sandbox they must join via the Twilio “join <code>” message first.
# The join starts the 24-hour session; test without a template during that window.
# Messages outside the window need an approved template and registered sender.
# Provider delivery status callbacks require TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN even when API-key auth sends messages.
#
# =============================================================================
#
# Dev-only: OTP bypass pin in development (defaults to "1234").
# Always disabled in NODE_ENV=production. Set empty to disable in dev:
# LOGIN_OTP_DEMO_CODE=
# LOGIN_OTP_DEMO_CODE=1234

# =============================================================================
# Resend — Forgot password emails (optional in dev; required in production API)
# Dashboard: https://resend.com/api-keys
# Without RESEND_API_KEY, local dev prints the reset URL in the backend terminal only.
# Staff-authenticated POST /api/messaging/email (invoice HTML from billing) uses the same key.
#
# Example:
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
#
# MAIL_FROM must use a verified domain in Resend (DNS), e.g. support@yourdomain.com after setup.
# Until your domain is verified you can use Resend's test sender format:
# MAIL_FROM=My Detail OS <onboarding@resend.dev>
#
# Development: if MAIL_FROM uses an unverified domain, the API retries once with onboarding@resend.dev
# (see resend-send.ts). Production sends only from MAIL_FROM — verify DNS before going live.
#
# Trial mode: Resend may only deliver to YOUR Resend-login email until you verify a domain at
# https://resend.com/domains — then you can mail any customer address.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# SaaS platform (branch limits + YOUR vendor login)
# =============================================================================
# Header X-Platform-Admin-Key for /api/platform/* (automation / CLI).
# PLATFORM_ADMIN_API_KEY=dev-platform-admin-key-change-me
#
# YOUR PLATFORM_OWNER account (not for customers).
# On Render free (no Shell): set these env vars and redeploy — API creates/updates the user on boot.
# PLATFORM_OWNER_EMAIL=you@yourcompany.com
# PLATFORM_OWNER_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-strong-secret
# PLATFORM_OWNER_NAME=Platform Owner
# PLATFORM_OWNER_PHONE=+919999999998
# PLATFORM_OWNER_ENSURE_ON_BOOT=true
# PLATFORM_OWNER_SYNC_PASSWORD=true
#
# Local defaults if unset: admin@mydetailos.com / Test@12345
# Or from your laptop against prod DB: DATABASE_URL="…" npm run saas:ensure-platform-owner
#
# Optional default CTAs on subscription seed:
# DEFAULT_CONTACT_US_URL=mailto:support@yourdomain.com?subject=Support
# DEFAULT_CONTACT_PHONE=+919876543210
# DEFAULT_UPGRADE_URL=mailto:support@yourdomain.com?subject=Upgrade%20plan
# (Avoid example.com and opening mailto with target=_blank — the app handles mailto safely.)
